From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Ericson <John.Ericson@Obsidian.Systems>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 20:06:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] tools/sgs: build the native link-editor on a non-illumos host

`usr/src/tools/sgs` already exists to build a *native* `ld` -- the one an
illumos-on-illumos cross-build uses, because only illumos' link-editor can
read `$mapfile_version 2` mapfiles. Nixpkgs needs exactly that: GNU `ld`
cannot parse the mapfiles under `lib/libc`, so nothing that carries a
versioning mapfile can be linked without it.

Everything here assumed "native" still meant illumos. Making it true of a
glibc/Linux host:

- `tools/sgs/native/`: a small set of shims, force-included or found ahead of
  the host's headers. `native_compat.h` supplies the `_t` integer spellings,
  `boolean_t` and the `sysmacros.h` arithmetic that illumos' `<sys/types.h>`
  would have provided to the staged headers. `thread.h`/`synch.h` map the
  Solaris threads API onto pthreads -- staging illumos' own is not an option,
  they drag in `<sys/int_types.h>` and `<sys/time_impl.h>`, which collide
  head-on with the host libc. `sys/systeminfo.h` implements `sysinfo(2)` over
  `uname(2)`; note that the host's `sysinfo` is an unrelated Linux syscall, so
  illumos' header is deliberately *not* staged. `native_support.c` provides
  `link_ver_string`, `assfail3()` and `panic()`.

- `tools/sgs/include`: stage the further "ELF-y" headers this turns out to
  need, in the spirit of the list already there.

- `tools/sgs/Makefile.com`: empty the macros that feed illumos-`ld`-only
  options and mapfiles into `LDFLAGS`/`DYNFLAGS`, reduce the CTF/`mcs`/`strip`
  post-processing to no-ops, and restate `DYNFLAGS` so `-R` becomes GNU `ld`'s
  `-rpath`. This is the whole point of the exercise: the link-editor used to
  *build* this tree is not the one being built.

- `tools/sgs/libconv`: drop `corenote.o` (core-note decoding, needs procfs and
  the `<sys/tsol/label.h>` chain), `lddstub.o` (`dlinfo(RTLD_DI_ORIGIN)`,
  `resolvepath(2)`) and `vernote.o` (generated by ksh93 plus the illumos
  assembler); none are on `ld`'s path.

- `tools/sgs/ld`: drop `-lumem`. Nothing in `cmd/sgs` calls a `umem_*`
  interface -- `grep -r 'umem_' usr/src/cmd/sgs` is empty -- it is linked
  purely as a faster `malloc`.

- `tools/sgs/Makefile`: forward `$ROOTONBLD` and `$ONBLD_TOOLS` to the
  sub-makes when set, so this can be installed outside the in-tree proto area.

- `libld/common/debug.c`: `stderr` is not a constant expression on every libc,
  so initialise `dbg_ofile.fptr` on first use rather than statically.

`sgsmsg` also moves to a 64-bit build, since a 32-bit host libc is not
something a cross-build host necessarily has.
